    "result_text": "The full build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `initials` field on the owner API response so it returns the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nTwo changes, following the existing `displayName` pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (which generates `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `initials` via a small helper that takes the first character of each name, upper-cases it, and appends a dot. It safely skips null/empty names.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` test (`john`/`smith` \u2192 `J.S.`) passes, and the full suite builds successfully with no failures.",
